# RER SEO Principles

## Objective

Build local real-estate authority for Mumbai's Western Suburbs, especially Jogeshwari and genuinely served nearby markets. SEO should support discovery and enquiries.

Do not treat specific keyword lists or a full location-page architecture as approved until that phase.

## Technical

Prefer server-rendered content, semantic HTML, unique titles/descriptions, canonicals, crawlable routes, sitemap, robots.txt, optimized images, descriptive alt text, accessible headings, fast pages, and structured data only when it fits.

Do not use hash links as stand-ins for important SEO pages.

Property URLs should eventually be `/properties/[slug]`, one unique URL per listing.

## On-page

One clear H1 where appropriate; logical H2/H3. Do not pick headings only for visual size.

Important pages should eventually have unique title, description, canonical, and Open Graph. Do not copy one generic metadata block onto every route.

## Local and properties

Mention Jogeshwari, Andheri, Goregaon, Lokhandwala, and other served areas only where true. No keyword stuffing. No location pages unless RER actually serves that place.

Property pages need unique copy, details, metadata, and alt text. Do not duplicate descriptions across listings.

## Schema, links, performance

Later, consider LocalBusiness / agent, Organization, BreadcrumbList, and listing schema only if accurate. Do not add schema for its own sake.

Internal links should help people as well as crawlers.

Do not trade performance for SEO theatre: optimized images, little client JS, Server Components, efficient fonts, few extra dependencies.

Never invent reviews, stats, awards, market claims, property facts, or experience.
